{
  "metadata": {
    "name": "picrawler L1 nav \u2014 CONTROL (wrong_sign)",
    "description": "L1 NAV, STAGE 1. The deployed imufused gait UNTOUCHED, plus a navigation layer that steers it. Chain: purple pixel AREA (reality.proprio.beacon, an honest colour test at full ray resolution -- NOT the old collider-identity oracle) -> RunTumbleNavV2 -> percept.klino_heading (an egocentric unit vector) -> MotorEPM.goal_bearing_topic, which replaces the heading PD's implicit spawn-bearing setpoint. The PD becomes the nav layer's ACTUATOR, not its competitor: the D term and the variance collapse it produced are untouched. NOT via nav_gain/target_compass -- nav_on gates the entire heading PD off plus the forward facing gate. RunTumbleNavV2 (not Klinotaxis) because it is the module the Cell actually deploys: n=20, 1.9 eats vs a 0.9 random-walk floor, 10 unit tests, 4 shipped ablation arms. Its eat_topic calibrates CONFIDENCE only; the policy is reward-free. Requires the camera: OGMA_PICRAWLER_PUBLISH_VISION=1 and a target_mode curriculum. \u26a0 nav_gain=0.0 IS LOAD-BEARING: with the target_compass oracle live, nav_on gates the ENTIRE heading PD off (both P and D) and hold_steer becomes 0 \u2014 the goal_bearing setpoint is then computed and DISCARDED. Measured 2026-08-04: with nav_gain=5.0 the purple-vs-neutral A/B was byte-identical on 4/4 seeds despite gb_msgs=5999. Zeroing nav_gain both removes the oracle and restores the PD the nav layer steers.",
    "env_target": "picrawler",
    "gym_mode": "corridor",
    "phase_tag": "motor-epm (minimal/deploy)",
    "derived_from_manifest": false,
    "episode_length": 6000,
    "mc_episode_period": 1500,
    "stability_gain": 0.05,
    "stability_y_norm": 0.5,
    "stability_speed": 0.05,
    "reward_shape": "trapezoid",
    "target_height": 0.085,
    "height_penalty_grace": 0.02,
    "height_penalty_scale": 0.03,
    "height_penalty_gain": 0.05,
